ions + `super.img` (`11/11` chunks in `210.140s`) + `erase cache` + `erase userdata` + `fastboot reboot`.\n3. **Diagnosed the Exact Root Cause Why the Box Has Green LED On and No HDMI Signal (`task-1188` & `task-1195`):**\n   - Compared SHA-256 hashes of [`programa perfecto/5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2/`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2) vs [`normal/B866V2/`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/normal/B866V2) vs [`V2/B866v2 Android 12/B866v2 Android 12/B866V2/`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/V2/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866V2) and inspected [`5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2/env_unlocked.img`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2/env_unlocked.img).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings (CRITICAL ROOT CAUSE OF GREEN LED + NO VIDEO / NO BOOT)\nOur SHA-256 audit (`task-1188` and `task-1195`) and inspection of `5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\env_unlocked.img` revealed **3 fatal bugs** in what `ProgramaPerfecto.cs` flashed compared to the working `normal\\B866V2-FlashATV12 - Evoca.bat`:\n\n1. **Fatal Bug #1 (Primary Cause of Green LED + Zero HDMI + No Boot): `[1/12] fastboot flash env env_unlocked.img` destroyed the box's real U-Boot `/dev/block/env` partition!**\n   - In `normal\\B866V2-FlashATV12 - Evoca.bat` (the original working EVOCA script), **`env` is NEVER flashed!** It only runs `fastboot oem 'setenv lock 10100000;save`, which modifies the single `lock=10100000` variable inside the box's genuine ZTE U-Boot environment while preserving all 100+ native ZTE/Amlogic U-Boot scripts (`bootsys`, `init_display`, `storeargs`, `upgrade_check`, `bcb_cmd`, `recovery_from_flash`, etc.).\n   - In contrast, `ProgramaPerfecto.cs` ran `[1/12] fastboot flash env env_unlocked.img`, which overwrote `/dev/block/env` with a synthetic 38-line file created from `uboot_env_franklin_b866v2.cfg` (`bootcmd=run storeboot`, `storeboot=imgread kernel boot ${loadaddr}; bootm ${loadaddr};`).\n   - Why does that synthetic `env_unlocked.img` brick the boot with a solid green LED and no HDMI?\n     - **No HDMI initialization:** It has no `init_display` command (`hdmitx hpd; osd open; vout output ${outputmode}`), so U-Boot never powers on the HDMI transmitter (`hdmitx`)!\n     - **No `storeargs` / `bootsys`:** On ZTE B866V2 (`INFORME_SESION_FASTBOOT_WATCHDOG_Y_SOLUCION.md` line 59), ZTE's U-Boot uses `ztebsp: bootcmd=bootsys` and `storeargs` to pass `vout=1080p60hz,enable hdmitx=,420,12bit androidboot.dynamic_partitions=true androidboot.dtbo_idx=0 androidboot.boot_devices=ffe07000.emmc` to the kernel. Because `env_unlocked.img` set `bootcmd=run storeboot` without running `storeargs`, `bootm ${loadaddr}` boots the Android 12 kernel with **empty `bootargs`**, so the kernel has no `vout`, no `androidboot.boot_devices=ffe07000.emmc`, and no `androidboot.dynamic_partitions=true`, hanging silently with the green power LED on!\n     - **No `upgrade_check` in `bootcmd`:** Because `bootcmd=run storeboot` skips `run upgrade_check`, U-Boot doesn't run `factory_update_param.aml` from `bootcmd`!\n\n2. **Fatal Bug #2: `5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\recovery.img` (`9AE79A6F88D0E541`) is NOT the original `normal\\B866V2\\recovery.img` (`497B76DF356F457C`)!**\n   - Look at `task-1195`:\n     - `normal\\B866V2\\recovery.img` has SHA-256 `497B76DF356F457C`.\n     - `V2\\B866v2 Android 12\\...\\recovery.img` has SHA-256 `7CB3D56D3200966B`.\n     - `5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\recovery.img` has SHA-256 `9AE79A6F88D0E541` (a modified/patched recovery image!).\n   - And `5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\cache_ext4.img` (`64 MB`) was flashed to `cache` (`1000 MB` partition) right before `fastboot erase cache`. In `normal\\B866V2-FlashATV12 - Evoca.bat`, `cache` is NEVER flashed with `cache_ext4.img`—only `fastboot erase userdata` and `fastboot erase cache` are run!\n\n3. **How to Rescue the Box (`Z41221040106995` and `Z41220110063684`) 100% Externally (Zero Screws / Zero TTL) & Fix `ProgramaPerfecto.cs` Permanently:**\n   - **How the box enters USB mode BEFORE U-Boot reads `bootcmd` from `/dev/block/env`:**\n     1. **Hardware Reset Button (`GPIOAO_3 == 0`) in U-Boot board_init_r / preboot (`InUsbBurn` / `VID_1B8E` WorldCup):**\n        - Look at [`INFORME_FORENSE_UART_TTL_SMARTTY_REA.md`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/13_CAPTURA_UART_TTL_SMARTTY/INFORME_FORENSE_UART_TTL_SMARTTY_REA.md) lines 27–31:\n          In Amlogic G12A U-Boot (`board_late_init` in C code, **before** `bootcmd` is executed!), U-Boot checks hardware pin `GPIOAO_3` (the external `RESET` pinhole button):\n          ```\n          gpio: pin GPIOAO_3 (gpio 3) value is 0\n          detect upgrade key\n          InUsbBurn\n          ```\n        - When `GPIOAO_3 == 0` (holding the external `RESET` button while plugging in power with the USB Male-to-Male cable connected to the PC), U-Boot C code enters **`InUsbBurn` (`WorldCup Device`, `VID_1B8E&PID_C003`)** BEFORE running `bootcmd`!\n        - And in `WorldCup` (`InUsbBurn`), `update.exe` can execute:\n          - `update.exe bulkcmd \"defenv_reserv; setenv lock 10100000; setenv otg_device 1; saveenv\"` (which restores the 100% genuine factory U-Boot environment compiled inside U-Boot RAM — including `bootsys`, `init_display`, `storeargs`, `upgrade_check` — and saves it to `/dev/block/env`!)\n          - `update.exe bulkcmd \"fastboot\"` (which puts the box straight into `U-Boot Fastboot` `PID_0D02`!)\n     2. **Also in `Fastboot` (`PID_0D02`):**\n        - In `U-Boot Fastboot`, running:\n          - `fastboot oem \"defenv_reserv; setenv lock 10100000; setenv otg_device 1; saveenv\"` or `fastboot erase env` (when `/dev/block/env` is erased, U-Boot on next boot sees an invalid CRC32 in `/dev/block/env` and automatically loads its built-in default environment from `bootloader.img` with `init_display`, `bootsys`, `storeargs`!).\n        - Let's verify what commands U-Boot `cb_oem_cmd` supports by decompressing `BL33` inside `normal\\B866V2\\bootloader.img` (or checking `fastboot erase env` / `fastboot oem \"defenv\"`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: `ForEach-Object -Parallel` failed in Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`task-1074` follow-up):**\n  - *Root cause:* `-Parallel` is PowerShell 7+ only.\n  - *Fix:* Used inline C# `Parallel.For` via `Add-Type`.\n- **Error 2: Box `Z41221040106995` stayed on solid green LED with no HDMI signal after completing the 13-partition flash:**\n  - *Root cause:* `[1/12] fastboot flash env env_unlocked.img` overwrote the box's `/dev/block/env` partition with a synthetic 38-line config (`bootcmd=run storeboot`) that lacks `init_display` (so HDMI never turns on) and lacks `storeargs` / `bootsys` (so the kernel boots with empty `bootargs` and hangs with the green LED on). Additionally, `5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\recovery.img` differed from `normal\\B866V2\\recovery.img`.\n  - *Fix to apply immediately:*\n    1. **NEVER flash `env_unlocked.img` to `env`!** Delete/remove `env` and `cache_ext4.img` from `partitionsToInject` in [`ProgramaPerfecto.cs`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR/ProgramaPerfecto.cs) and in `TryCatchWorldCup48ms()`.\n    2. Copy the genuine [`normal/B866V2/recovery.img`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/normal/B866V2/recovery.img) (`SHA256: 497B76DF356F457C`) into `5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\recovery.img` and `V2\\B866v2 Android 12\\B866v2 Android 12\\B866V2\\recovery.img` so all `.img` files match the exact working `normal\\B866V2` set.\n    3. Add automatic `env` repair to both `TryCatchWorldCup48ms()` (`update.exe bulkcmd \"defenv_reserv; setenv -f lock 10100000; setenv otg_device 1; saveenv\"` + `update.exe bulkcmd \"fastboot\"`) and Fastboot (`fastboot erase env` + `fastboot oem 'setenv lock 10100000;save` + `fastboot reboot bootloader`) so that any box whose `env` was overwritten by `env_unlocked.img` immediately recovers its